-11-21T13:17:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T13:20:59Z"},{"id":775649602,"node_id":"RA_kwDORF9GhM4uO3lC","name":"nanobot_ai-0.4.2.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"Re-bin","id":52506698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA2Njk4","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/x-gtar","state":"uploaded","size":12511410,"digest":"sha256:a2ca0ab20e3604debfc01c783dc17155cbe58ce85e8064864a1e2f79ffabad33","download_count":10,"created_at":"2026-11-21T13:18:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T13:19:47Z"},{"id":775655342,"node_id":"RA_kwDORF9GhM4uO4-u","name":"release-manifest.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"Re-bin","id":52506698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA2Njk4","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":3036,"digest":"sha256:5326bab4ca5ae7b4924cd1e373420a5bebb2b9ef8da3af5043057e6bed2af2e9","download_count":9,"created_at":"2026-11-21T13:21:02Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T13:21:02Z"}],"body":"## Changes\n\n- Connect over SSH to gateways that also advertise a public WebSocket URL. **Use existing SSH settings** now supports Windows hosts where Python 3 is available as `python`. The quick-pairing command remains Linux-only; gateway-native TLS and `trustedProxyAuth` are still unsupported over SSH. [#6682](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6682)\n- See the latest activity when a turn is collapsed, and see which follow-up messages are still waiting for the agent. Reconnecting also preserves the state of running turns more reliably. [#6664](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6664), [#6719](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6719), [#6726](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6726), [#6715](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6715)\n- Find Tools, Skills, and Chat Platforms in one **Apps** catalog. Choose the reasoning effort for your next message from the composer, without changing the shared preset. [#6700](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6700), [#6441](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6441)\n- Long messages you send can collapse to keep the conversation easier to scan. Expand them with **Show more**, or copy the full text without expanding. [#6739](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6739)\n- Align the footer controls in the settings sidebar, and keep the model picker open when you reopen it quickly after switching presets. [Settings sidebar fix](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/commit/bc690f0394a00703d6f25a48c63ecb0170b2e091), [#6743](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6743)\n- Dream can organize detailed knowledge in a Markdown wiki and keep a short memory summary in context. Existing memory files and custom Dream guides remain supported. [#4477](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/4477)\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n- For a manual update, stop nanobot, back up your configuration and workspace, and update the gateway using the original installation method. If you use a separate WebUI client with a remote gateway, update both to the same version. [Update guide](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/0dc8679edcc6061fbcdf3de13c7e16000e9d1b65/docs/updating.md#installation-owners)\n- **Standalone API server:** `nanobot serve`, its `/v1` endpoints, and the `nanobot-api` Compose service are retired. Stop the old process or container before upgrading and keep the data volumes. There is no drop-in HTTP replacement. The gateway, WebUI, Python SDK, and outbound model connections still work; old API conversations can be read through the Python SDK. [#6614](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6614)\n- **OpenAI provider settings:** If you explicitly selected an API using the old `apiType` or `api_type` setting, save your configuration with v0.4.1 before upgrading, or migrate to the current `api` field. Update any old launcher environment variables separately. The old default `auto` needs no action. [#6615](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6615)\n- **Global shared session:** `unifiedSession` and `unified_session` are now ignored. Existing session data stays in place; new messages use per-chat or explicitly selected topic routes. [#6621](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/pull/6621)\n- This release supports manual installation. In-app automatic updates are not enabled for it.\n"}
